FATAL_OBJECTIONS: [
  "Mem0 (arXiv:2504.19413) is a direct, unrebutted collision: it performs write-path dedup/merge of redundant memories and beats full-history AND recency baselines on LOCOMO — the exact positive claim of CLAIM-0041. Corroborated by A-MEM (arXiv:2502.12110) for write-path consolidation. Two independent sources confirm the collision (anti-hallucination rule satisfied).",
  "Redis Agent Memory Server ships the proposed mechanism as production code: store-time semantic vector-search dedup with a configurable distance threshold before indexing, with E2E tests for paraphrase merging — the systems contribution is already deployed open-source (systems_reviewer, unrebutted).",
