PRIOR_ART_ADEQUATE: no
RATIONALE: Three of five reviewers vote RED with fatal objections that are unrebutted by evidence. The prior-art search is severely inadequate: the packet's caveat names only MemGPT/Letta, Generative-Agents, and read-path RAG dedup, entirely missing the most direct collision — Mem0 (arXiv:2504.19413), which performs write-path memory dedup/merge and demonstrates downstream recall improvements over recency baselines on LOCOMO. Also missing: A-MEM (arXiv:2502.12110, write-path consolidation), Redis Agent Memory Server (shipping production implementation of the exact mechanism), MemoryBank (arXiv:2305.10250, forgetting-curve eviction baseline), LOCOMO benchmark (arXiv:2402.17753), and foundational cache-replacement theory (Belady 1966; ARC, Megiddo & Modha 2003). Per the area chair rule, GREEN is impossible with inadequate prior-art AND unrebutted REDs.

Synthesizing by evidence, not vote-count: (1) The novelty_killer's Mem0 collision is the load-bearing finding — the positive mechanism (write-path dedup beats recency at matched recall) is already published AND demonstrated on a real benchmark, with corroboration from A-MEM and a shipping Redis implementation. The packet's surviving delta (cheap no-LLM gate) is where L0's own results are weakest. (2) The theory_skeptic's tautology argument is independently fatal for Part (A) — amplification = re-store rate is a measurement of the input parameter, not a discovery. (3) The evaluation_prosecutor and product_realist correctly identify that the size-cap baseline is a strawman: real agent-memory systems use importance-weighted eviction, which retains critical old facts without the false-dedup risk of a threshold-tuned gate, rendering the claimed advantage moot against the actual deployed alternative.

The two YELLOW votes (evaluation_prosecutor, product_realist) do not rebut these fatal objections — they raise the SAME concerns (strawman baseline, conditional/knob-tuned win, missing importance-weighted eviction) and diverge from RED only by acknowledging the negative characterization has operational value. I agree the negative finding is honest and well-reported (the researcher flagged the saturation artifact, the threshold sensitivity, and the 18/108 loss configs), but an honest negative that recovers known cache-replacement theory against a strawman baseline, while missing the most direct prior work, does not clear the bar for advancement. The orchestrator note anticipated this outcome and instructed: converge and move to the next fresh area. Prompt version: v001.
